															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/carboncore" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1304641); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1304641&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609513673" alt="carbonCore" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1304641)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/carboncore" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1304641); return false;" >carbonCore</a></span> <span class="odate time_1332455565 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Mar 2012 22:32</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1400277">
									

<p>They will not have the same DNA as the host. The reason they are growing abnormally is because of a mutation in cell DNA. Normally a cell will try to repair any DNA damage done to it, but if it divides before it can do so, the mutation is passed on to the next cell. That next cell begins dividing uncontrollably due to the mutation it carried from the parent cell &#8212; it considers its DNA proper at that point and will not attempt to repair it.</p>

							</div>

								
					
