														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1407931">
									

<p>Whilst what you said is technically true, a cancer can be caused by as little as 2 single base point mutations in some cases, making it basically the same as host tissue. A cell may also contain more than 100 point mutation and still operate the same as normal, it all depends on the exact locations on the genome. i mean you could simply say its done though an unknown means, 'cos ya know, its an SCP so that works.</p>

